{"id": "EUVD-2026-76302", "enisaUuid": "00d32e07-ba33-3e25-855f-e546bb34a693", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: unregister the connection before draining the rx tasklet\n\nsmc_conn_free() calls smc_ism_unset_conn() only while the link group is\nstill on its device list, and never sets conn->killed.\nsmc_lgr_terminate_sched() unlinks the group immediately and defers killing\nits connections to a work item, so a connection freed in that window keeps\nits smcd->conn[] slot with both gates in smcd_handle_irq() open, and the\ndevice can re-arm the receive tasklet after tasklet_kill() has returned. On\nthe DMB-nocopy path the ghost send buffer is freed right after that drain,\nso the re-armed tasklet dereferences it.\n\nUnregister unconditionally and drain before the detach at both teardown\nsites, mirroring rmb_desc, which smc_buf_unuse() releases after the drain.\nClear conn->sndbuf_desc before freeing it as well, so a reader that samples\nthe pointer cannot get one that is already freed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:03", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6b6ac713ee82b340a8e3be30b101bd2840deec4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b4d540ac95cd35c6ebab6afb7eae2bcac7b277a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bd8b764a610b6b6bc0c4d3d01652747f6e0b5c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b74d313567dfc1b7e56629ddbad04e728686f235", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36cdf5d48ca191dcd71c28cadbe0981b1d25318d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80979", "GHSA-3r27-v3q5-phcc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0644164c-81ae-3519-a17a-5ec793648701", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "0a4ef33d-fedc-3c0e-b6ad-bb5d915ccabc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae2be35cbed2c8385e890147ea321a3fcc3ca5fa <36cdf5d48ca191dcd71c28cadbe0981b1d25318d"}, {"id": "265d650d-4b01-33b9-b438-4983457e022a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "3a7ac856-d28e-3a1a-aa36-122cad667c0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.66 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "5dc0d815-b3f7-353f-aaf5-f445702d4360", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae2be35cbed2c8385e890147ea321a3fcc3ca5fa <5bd8b764a610b6b6bc0c4d3d01652747f6e0b5c3"}, {"id": "743af1bc-e715-3c94-af0c-2e50cfa971e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "886e5807-ed6d-3a37-8ba1-889342be1b1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "21f6f41e82e59740e26e06e77bdf58dc7f6f08dd <b6b6ac713ee82b340a8e3be30b101bd2840deec4"}, {"id": "8cfa2d11-e969-3480-99ec-b9ec065242b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "ad35dca3-a6ea-3591-a05b-85cf73142b7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae2be35cbed2c8385e890147ea321a3fcc3ca5fa <b74d313567dfc1b7e56629ddbad04e728686f235"}, {"id": "bbf5b012-0e39-3f1d-a787-ea7835cec28e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "c4685cde-e0c3-3ad4-9988-9abf32340283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e5aba205-4437-3594-8fe8-7217bfca6d65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f7666f28-215b-3b8d-aae2-60734af0c84d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae2be35cbed2c8385e890147ea321a3fcc3ca5fa <b4d540ac95cd35c6ebab6afb7eae2bcac7b277a5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b1aa4c64-801f-3de7-88a